KNOWNBUG
nonansi_port4.sv
--bound 2
^\[main\.p0\] .*: PROVED up to bound 2$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
A syntax error. In the module body, bus i; cannot be told apart from
the declaration of a variable of a user-defined type, or from the start of
an interface instantiation, before elaboration; an interface port
declaration with a modport, bus.sink i;, is accepted. The parser would
need to accept the declaration as a data declaration, and the type checker
would need to turn it into an interface port when bus is an interface
and i is in the port list.
